{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Upon</b> — Even though upon the back of <b>they plowed</b> [refers to] plowers. And the meaning: disgrace and lowliness, in the manner of: \"and you made your back like the ground\" [Isaiah 51:23]." "<b>For they made long</b> — From the same root as in <b>half a ma'aneh</b> [1 Samuel 13:21]." "<b>The meaning of cut</b> — Just as one cuts the rope, they will not be able to plow upon the back. And the meaning is that HaShem will remove their yoke from upon the shoulders of Israel, by cutting off their kingdom."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 129, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes גוך from Isaiah 51:23; the Masoretic text reads גוּךְ (your back).", 1 "Ibn Ezra derives למעניתם from the root ענה in the sense 'to sharpen/gouge,' as in the file (מחרשה/פים/מעדה) of 1 Samuel 13:21; the exact derivation and comparison is compressed and the identification of מענה is debated among commentators."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:29.900181030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}